  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1002 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThe upper ridge is expected to build more fully overhead through\nthe weekend, suppressing deeper moisture and convective chances\nwhile allowing temperatures to climb further. Friday through\nSunday will be the hottest stretch. Highs are forecast in the\nupper 90s for many locations west of the Plateau, with the NBM and\nensemble guidance showing a solid chance (around 80% for the\nNashville area) of reaching or exceeding 100 deg on Saturday and\nSunday. Prolonged heat indices of 105-110+ combined with warm\novernight lows in the 70s will produce major to extreme heat risk.\nThe Heat Advisory is already extending through Friday evening and\nwill likely need further extension or expansion depending on\ntrends. \n\nPrecipitation chances drop to low or near zero Friday through the\nweekend as the ridge dominates. Any isolated activity would be\ndiurnally driven and limited. Early next week, guidance indicates\nthe ridge begins to shift or weaken as a boundary approaches from\nthe north, which should bring modest cooling and a return of\nhigher rain chances later in the period. Exact timing of the\npattern change remains somewhat uncertain beyond early next week,\nbut the multi-day heat wave itself has good support across\ndeterministic and ensemble guidance. \n\nResidents should continue heat safety measures: limit outdoor\nactivity during peak heating hours, stay hydrated, check on\nvulnerable individuals, and never leave people or pets in\nvehicles.",
